======================================================================
Universal Constant-Leading-Form Mechanism
======================================================================

Inductive step: E_{k-1} chart (u,v), blow up p_k=(u0,0), u0!=0.
New chart: u = u0 + u'*v', v = v'.

Pullback of monomial (schematic):
  PULL = (u0 + u'*v')^{-J} * (v')^{-N} * U(u',v')
  where U is a unit (regular, nonzero at v'=0).

Coefficient of (v')^{-m}: set v'=0.
  (u0 + u'*v')^{-J} at v'=0:
    = u0^{-J}.
  INDEPENDENT of u'.

  U(u',v') at v'=0:
    = U(u',0). For the LEADING (lowest v') term, U contributes
    only its constant part (in v'), which may depend on u'.

======================================================================
Symbolic verification of the evaluation
======================================================================

(u0 + u'*v')^{-2} expanded, v'=0 coefficient:
  u0**(-2)
  Depends on u': False

Indeed: (u0)^{-J}, constant in u'.

======================================================================
Contrast: FIRST blowup (u0 = 0)
======================================================================

(u'*v')^{-2} = u'^{-2} * v'^{-2}.
The u'-dependence SURVIVES. Leading form CAN depend on u'.
This is why E1 (first exceptional) is exempt from the theorem.

======================================================================
Theorem statement and consequence
======================================================================

THEOREM: For k>=2, with all centers u0 != 0, the (v')^{-m}
coefficient on E_k is independent of the residual transverse
coordinate u', for every m>=1.

COROLLARY: [phi0^P : phi0^Q] is constant (degree 0) on E_k.
For m>=2, the dicritical condition deg=m is IMPOSSIBLE.

Therefore: NO exceptional divisor E_k (k>=2) obtained by
successive blowups at nonzero centers can carry a dicritical
of order m>=2.

This single mechanism explains ALL the specific results:
  - Two-branch bridge (E2): constant.
  - Leaf E3, E4: constant.
  - Middle E2: constant.
  - General E_k, k>=2: constant.

The only possible dicriticals with m>=2 would have to live on
E1 (the first exceptional), where u0=0 and transverse dependence
survives. But E1 is a single divisor; it cannot form a pair,
and a solitary m>=2 on E1 is constrained by global degree bounds.
